# File: .dockerignore
# Purpose: build-context filter for every deploy image (context = repo root):
#   deploy/docker/{go,admin,storefront}.Dockerfile. Keeps the context small and makes sure no
#   VCS data, local env files, keys, evidence or dependency trees reach an image layer.
# Runs as/in: read by `docker build` on the build host (deploy/scripts/build-images.sh).
# Reads env / secrets: none. Secrets never live in the repo checkout (see deploy/README.md).
# Used by: all image builds. Depends on: nothing.
# Status: DESIGN; verified by smoke S06 (required patterns present) and S07 (builds).
# Change rules: images only COPY go.mod/go.sum, cmd, internal, migrations, deploy/tools,
#   package manifests, apps/*, packages/*, scripts/dev/package-admin.mjs. Do not exclude those.
#   .git is excluded, so Go builds use -buildvcs=false and the revision goes into OCI labels.

# VCS, agent and editor state
.git
.github
.codex
.claude
.impeccable
.worktrees
.local
**/.DS_Store

# Dependency trees and build output (rebuilt inside the image from the lockfile)
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/*.tsbuildinfo
bin
coverage.out

# Test output, evidence and docs that images never need
deploy/.evidence
evidence
experiments
output
test-results
playwright-report
tests
docs
contracts

# Local configuration and anything that could hold a secret
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
deploy/env/*.env
**/*.local.*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.crt
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
**/secrets
**/*.dump
